  "importedChanges": [
    "Retain the Pi process identity for process-based integrations while keeping Rotom command and UI branding",
    "model picker and scoped-model configuration use consistent name-first labels (source, tests, docs)",
    "model picker display names and picker-local thinking level selection (source, tests, docs)",
    "Replace recorded session fixtures with synthetic compaction input; omit unused before-compaction transcript",
    "Retain Rotom branding, startup, product updates, session ID, Qoder metering/catalog and abort/compaction fixes across the 1.0.4 merge",
    "Merge v1.1.0 over the 1.0.4 fork; earlier selective 1.1.0 backports are now part of the base",
    "Retain upstream classifier models/APIs, virtual model routing and the built-in MCP extension; Rotom adds no classifier or virtual model of its own",
    "Merge v1.3.0 over the 1.1.0 fork; upstream removed the experimental client/protocol/server stack and the chord runtime dependency",
    "Settle aborted turns locally instead of dispatching a provider request with an aborted signal; expose pi.appendUsage for extension-made model requests",
    "Merge v1.4.0; retain Rotom compaction metrics, concurrent split summaries, context projection, connection recovery and Codemode direct-only boundaries",
    "Honour Retry-After / retry-after-ms on 429 within the agent delay cap, and treat quota, balance and 402 failures as non-retryable with one actionable hint",
    "Keep the head and the tail of tool results and bound tool call arguments when serializing history for compaction summaries",
    "Merge v1.5.2 over the 1.4.0 fork; pi-schema joins the runtime packages and replaces TypeBox validation of tool arguments",
    "Keep cacheWarming at \"streaming\" and Anthropic message threads opt-in (compat.supportsMessageThreads) instead of the upstream 1.5.1 defaults",
    "Retain name-first model picker labels, connect-failure cause tagging, bash error codes, edit no-write receipts and head+tail summary truncation across the 1.5.2 merge"
  ],
